#: ../../ops/backup.rst:150
msgid "What a restore does to the network"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:152
msgid ""
"A hub signs a notice that confirms the current key state of each agent. "
"After a restore, the hub's database may be older than the key histories "
"that nodes have since published. To prevent an old key from being "
"confirmed as current, the hub signs no notice for an agent until"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:157
msgid "it accepts a strictly longer key history for the agent from its node, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:158
msgid ""
"30 minutes have passed since the hub began to serve and the node sends a "
"request signed with the key at the top of the stored history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:161
msgid ""
"Each agent is released on its own. Nodes report ``Your hub was just "
"restored from a backup and is checking identity records; nothing to do, "
"it takes at most 30 minutes.`` An owner who is online is released within "
"seconds. An agent that rotated after the backup and whose node stays "
"offline remains held until it connects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:167
msgid ""
"The same quarantine applies if ``hub.db`` is put back by hand: at the "
"next start the hub finds that its change counter is lower than the one in"
" ``kel_hwm`` and holds every agent in the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:171
msgid ""
"Mailboxes are empty after a restore. A sender asks the hub whether an "
"envelope was collected; the hub answers ``unknown`` for an envelope it no"
" longer has, and the sender's node sends the message again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:175
msgid ""
"After a restore, nodes can compare their own payment record with the "
"hub's ledger with ``anet reconcile`` and check the supply chain with "
"``anet audit-hub`` (see :ref:`reference-cli`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:180
msgid "When the hub identity itself is lost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/backup.rst:182
msgid ""
"If the data directory is lost together with ``hub_identity.kel``, the hub"
" cannot be continued under its AID by copying files. A new data directory"
" creates a new identity, which is a new hub: new network name, empty "
"ledger, and peers that must list its new AID. If the recovery file and "
"passphrase are available, a rotation under them proves control of the "
"identity; see :ref:`ops-hub-recovery`."
msgstr ""

